# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Abstrekkt handoff bundle
#
# ⚠ THIS REPO MUST STAY PRIVATE.
#
# It intentionally contains clinical records (SPECT renders, Amen Clinics
# eval, CPT-3 / TBR assessments), memoir source material, a police incident
# report, and personal identifiers including an SSN fragment, DOB, home
# addresses, and family names.
#
# Basis: Kyle Rosebrook authorized inclusion of his own clinical data and
# attested on 2026-07-16 that the third-party details (family, police report)
# are cleared. That authorization covers THIS private repo only — it is not a
# clearance to make the repo public, mirror it, or fork it elsewhere.
#
# Note: project/abstrekkt/protections.js sets an `absent` policy for Kinsley.
# The raw sources here are broader than what that seal permits in rendered
# artifacts. The seal still governs anything built from this material.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Secrets — .env.example / templates stay tracked, real .env never does.
# Belt-and-suspenders: all three forms kept explicitly for cross-tool clarity
# (.env* is a superset, but .env and .env.* are listed for grep-ability).
.env
.env.*
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.*.template

# Hardened secret exclusions (2026-07-17) — ab-enablement-co held a live
# production-credential trove. Belt-and-suspenders so secrets can never stage.
# Updated 2026-07-19: added *.p12, *-env.txt after audit (see docs/SECURITY-AUDIT.md).
*.env                       # e.g. flashfusion-production.env, flashnframe_secrets.env
*-env.txt                   # e.g. Infinite-heroes-env.txt — env vars stored with .txt ext
**/Vault/
**/Secrets_files/
*secret*
*Secret*
*credential*
*Credential*
*CRED*
ssshhhh*
Backup-codes*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa*

# Dependencies / build output
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.turbo/
.wrangler/
*.tsbuildinfo

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
